  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1251 PM CDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nThe strong upper ridge will continue to collapse toward the east\nover the northern part of the country, but continue to control the\nweather over the southern states. Southeasterly low level flow\nwill keep hot, moist air over South-Central Texas. There may be\nsome seabreeze convection each day for the rest of the week over\nthe Coastal Plains, but chances are low. Most of the area will be\nhot and dry. Temperatures will be steady and above normal through\nthe week. The NBM is showing higher humidity for the middle and\nlatter part of the week, but it has tended to run moist in the\nmedium term. The forecast higher dewpoints have not been\nverifying. However, if the higher dewpoints do verify we will\nreach Heat Advisory criteria over the Coastal Plains and I-35\nCorridor by mid-week.",
